            <section id="work" class="entries">
                <h3>Recent Work</h3>

                <p class="section-intro"><span class="company-label">Mod Op, 2024&ndash;2026.</span> I was a founding member of Mod Op's Innovation team and led a team of six as VP, Creative Innovation, in the company's first product engineering group. Mod Op is a roughly 500-person agency that pledged $10M to proprietary AI. I helped design and build the platform underneath Orion, its AI operating layer, and owned six products in the portfolio from concept through go-to-market, delivery, and refinement.</p>

                <p class="platform-feature">
                    <span class="feature-label">PLATFORM CASE STUDY</span>
                    <strong><a class="case-study-link" href="/nexus">Orion and Nexus: the AI operating layer</a></strong>
                    I led product vision and delivery for Nexus, the shared system underneath Orion. It gave the agency common data and knowledge foundations, agents that made that knowledge accessible and automation possible, and a chat harness that put those capabilities in everyone's hands securely.
                    <br />
                    <span class="fun-fact"><strong>95% employee adoption · 700+ agents deployed</strong> as of August 2026<br /><a href="https://digiday.com/marketing/build-or-buy-inside-indie-agency-mod-ops-ai-infrastructure/" target="_blank">Digiday put Orion's avoided licensing costs at roughly $3M</a> that same month.</span>
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong><a class="case-study-link" href="/nexus#cs-context">Brand Agents</a></strong> Persistent assistants grounded in a client's approved knowledge, voice, and goals, in use across agency and client work since April 2025. I helped shape the product and <a href="https://www.modop.com/blog/brand-agent-how-we-created-ai-that-actually-helps-clients/" target="_blank">wrote its launch story</a>. More than 200 client-specific Brand Agents were deployed by August 2026.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong><a class="case-study-link" href="/geo">GEO by Mod Op</a></strong> Brand visibility monitoring across the major AI platforms. It went live in June 2026, Mod Op <a href="https://www.modop.com/press/mod-op-launches-free-ai-search-visibility-tool-and-unveils-the-geo-50/" target="_blank">launched it publicly</a> in August 2026, and it is <a href="https://geo.modop.ai" target="_blank">live now</a>. I took the concept from idea through prototype into production, working with the agency's search and strategy experts to turn a weekslong manual audit into an automated free audit that leads into a paid program.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong><a class="case-study-link" href="/launchpad">Launchpad</a></strong> A rapid prototyping environment and product framework with access control, self-serve deployment, and feedback built in. It powered a cross-team hackathon program that paired non-technical teammates with innovation engineers and produced dozens of working prototypes between February and August 2026, and it became a transparent internal showcase of Mod Op's AI roadmap.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong><a class="case-study-link" href="/mod-heat">Mod Heat</a></strong> Brand-aware news and trend tracking, ranked by relevance, risk, and reach. I originated the concept, pitched it to the executive team, and shipped it with my team.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong>Audience Lab</strong> Digital-twin audience simulation, grounded in real customer and buyer data, for creative pretesting and strategy.
